---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, NETWORK_NAME } from '../../../site.config.mjs';
---

<SiteLayout title="Privacy and terms">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 md:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Privacy and terms</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Last updated <mark>[CHECK: date]</mark></p>

    <div class="prose-page">
      <p>
        <mark>[CHECK: this notice is modelled on the Australian Privacy Principles but is not legal advice. Consider
        asking a privacy officer at a partner institution to review it before launch.]</mark>
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy notice</h2>

      <h3>Who we are</h3>
      <p>
        This website is run by the leadership committee of the {NETWORK_NAME} ("we", "us"). You can contact us about
        privacy at any time at {CONTACT_EMAIL}.
      </p>

      <h3>What we collect</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Dataset listings:</strong> the description of the dataset, and the name, role and email address of its
          contact person.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Skills profiles:</strong> your name and title, role, career stage, institution, state, discipline,
          skills, short bio, ORCID iD, profile link, what you are looking for and open to, and your email address.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Messages sent through the site:</strong> the sender's name, email address and institution, and the
          message.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sign-in and membership:</strong> your email address, the details you give when requesting membership
          (name, institution, country, role and how you'll use the network), and any resources you share with members.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We don't use advertising or analytics cookies, and we don't sell or share your information for marketing.
        <mark>[CHECK]</mark>
      </p>

      <h3>Why we collect it</h3>
      <p>
        To publish approved listings, pass on messages between researchers, let you update or remove your listing, contact
        you about your listing, and ask each year whether it is still current.
      </p>

      <h3>Who can see it</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Once approved, everything in a listing <strong>except the email address</strong> is shown publicly.</li>
        <li>
          Email addresses are never shown on the site. Only the network's admins and our automated email system can see
          them.
        </li>
        <li>
          When you send a message through the site, we pass your name, email address, institution and message to the
          custodian or researcher you contacted, so they can reply to you directly.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Where it is stored</h3>
      <p>
        Listings and messages are stored in a database run by Supabase in Sydney, Australia. Emails are sent through a
        Google Gmail account, and Google may store email outside Australia. The website itself is hosted by GitHub Pages in
        the United States, which may record visitors' IP addresses for security. <mark>[CHECK]</mark>
      </p>

      <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
      <p>
        Listings are kept while they are published and deleted when you ask us to remove them or they are taken down.
        Messages sent through the site are kept for 12 months and then deleted. <mark>[CHECK: retention period]</mark>
      </p>

      <h3>Your choices</h3>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct, update or remove your information at any time by emailing {CONTACT_EMAIL}. You can
        also sign in with the email address on your listing to update or withdraw it yourself.
      </p>

      <h3>Complaints</h3>
      <p>
        If you have a concern about how we handle your information, email {CONTACT_EMAIL} and we will respond within 30
        days. If you are not satisfied, you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at
        oaic.gov.au.
      </p>

      <h2>Terms of use</h2>

      <h3>What a listing is</h3>
      <p>
        Listings describe data held by their custodians. The network does not hold, host or grant access to data, and a
        listing is not an endorsement. Custodians remain responsible for ethics approvals, participant consent and data
        agreements, and decide who may use their data.
      </p>

      <h3>What you must not submit</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Data files, or any part of a dataset.</li>
        <li>Anything that could identify a study participant.</li>
        <li>Information about a dataset or a person that you do not have permission to share.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Accuracy</h3>
      <p>
        The person who submits a listing is responsible for its accuracy. We may lightly edit listings for clarity, and may
        decline or remove any listing at our discretion.
      </p>

      <h3>Messages</h3>
      <p>
        Use the contact forms only for genuine research enquiries. We may block messages that are unsolicited marketing,
        abusive or automated.
      </p>

      <h3>Updating or removing a listing</h3>
      <p>
        Sign in with the email address on your listing and open My listings. Updates are checked by an admin before they go
        live; withdrawing a listing takes effect straight away. You can also email {CONTACT_EMAIL}.
      </p>

      <h3>No warranty</h3>
      <p>
        We provide this website as is, and do not guarantee that listings are complete, accurate or current.
        <mark>[CHECK]</mark>
      </p>

      <h3>Changes</h3>
      <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page shows when they last changed.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
